{"id":"lanes","ord":"a","title":"Lanes","desc":"What's live. One node per dispatched task; its children are the workflow steps, CLONED (real nodes, not mirrors) so each lane's marks are its own. The DAG is the `after` edges — the app draws blocked-vs-ready, and `set_doing` refuses on a blocked step, so the pipeline enforces itself. Facts a query can reach (`prop:agent=claude-opus`, `prop:terminal`) live as properties: `agent`/`repo`/`item` on the lane, `terminal` on the implement step, `pr` on the step that opened it. The lane's `item` names the repo-roadmap node it serves; the roadmap keeps the story, this file keeps the dispatch. PROTOTYPE (2026-08-15): hand-cloned from the pipeline in docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md — the workflows.olai template file comes once this shape is approved."}
